From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: undo a failed AP BSS add

wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add() links the new i802_bss into the driver and
stores it in *drv_priv before nl80211_setup_ap(). When that fails, the
function returns -1 and leaves both in place. The caller's cleanup then
takes the half set up BSS for its own: for an AP MLD BSS,
hostapd_cleanup_driver() calls driver_nl80211_link_remove() on a BSS
with no links, which copies the context of its unused first link (NULL)
into bss->ctx and reports EVENT_MLD_INTERFACE_FREED with it, and hostapd
crashes in hostapd_wpa_event(). A failure of nl80211_set_mode() leaks
the BSS.

Undo the add on both failures, as the other error paths of the function
do, and clear *drv_priv.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -9819,8 +9819,12 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add(voi
 		new_bss->added_if = added;
 
 		/* Set interface mode to NL80211_IFTYPE_AP */
-		if (nl80211_set_mode(new_bss, nlmode))
+		if (nl80211_set_mode(new_bss, nlmode)) {
+			if (added)
+				nl80211_remove_iface(drv, ifidx);
+			os_free(new_bss);
 			return -1;
+		}
 
 		if (bridge &&
 		    i802_check_bridge(drv, new_bss, bridge, ifname) < 0) {
@@ -9850,8 +9854,16 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add(voi
 		nl80211_init_bss(new_bss);
 
 		/* Subscribe management frames for this WPA_IF_AP_BSS */
-		if (nl80211_setup_ap(new_bss))
+		if (nl80211_setup_ap(new_bss)) {
+			drv->first_bss->next = new_bss->next;
+			if (drv_priv)
+				*drv_priv = NULL;
+			nl80211_destroy_bss(new_bss);
+			if (added)
+				nl80211_remove_iface(drv, ifidx);
+			os_free(new_bss);
 			return -1;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (drv->global)
